    3. For each row-pair, choose a unique row and two distinct columns with gap in [2,7]; ensure no column is reused by a col-pair endpoint.
    4. For each col-pair, choose a unique column and two distinct rows with gap in [2,7]; ensure no row is reused by a row-pair endpoint.
    5. Place unpaired markers on cells not sharing a row with a row-pair or column with a col-pair (so they remain singletons in their row/col).
    6. Verify all markers are isolated (no two adjacent); reject and retry if violated.
    7. Fill grid with background (0) and place marker pixels (8). Green must not appear.
